$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura Couplings
(Table 5). Arylboronic acid (0.75-1.00 mmol) and Pd(dtbpf)Cl2 (6.5 mg,
0.01 mmol) were added under an Ar atmosphere in a 5.0 mL microwave vial
with magnetic stir bar and Teflon-lined septum. Aryl bromide (0.50 mmol),
triethylamine (0.21 mL, 1.50 mmol), and surfactant solution (1.0 mL, 2 wt
% in degassed water) were sequentially added into the reaction under a
flow of Ar. The reaction was allowed to stir vigorously for 2-11 h. The
reaction mixture was then diluted with EtOAc, passed through a silica gel
bed, and further washed with EtOAc to collect the coupling product. All
volatile solvent was removed in vacuo to obtain crude product that was
further purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
3-(Thiophen-3-yl)quinoline (Table 5, entry 3). Following the general
procedure using 3-bromoquinoline (105 mg, 0.50 mmol) and
thiophen-3-ylboronic acid (96 mg, 0.75 mmol) the reaction was allowed to
stir for 4 h. After column chromatography, the product was obtained as a
white solid (102 mg, 95%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.25-9.20 (d, J =
2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.34-8.30 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 8.18-8.11 (d, J = 8.3 Hz,
1H), 7.90-7.85 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.75-7.70 (m, 1H), 7.70-7.67 (dd, J =
2.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.62-7.57 (m, 1H), 7.56-7.53 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.5 Hz, 1H),
7.53-7.50 (dd, J = 5.1, 2.9 Hz, 1H).32
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions (reagent)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM "Nok": A Phytosterol-Based Amphiphile Enabling Transition-Metal-Catalyzed
Couplings in Water at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Klumphu, Piyatida; Lipshutz, Bruce H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(3), 888-900

