$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure of isolation of 2a. To a screw-capped vial was added Pd(OAc)2
(3.4 mg, 0.015 mmol, 5 mol %), P(p-C6H4F)3 (9.5 mg, 0.03 mmol, 10 mol %),
CsOH.H2O (101 mg, 0.6 mmol, 2 eq), and boronate ester 1 (93 mg, 0.3 mmol,
1 eq). The vial was sealed with a PTFE septum and then evacuated and
backfilled with N2 (this sequence was carried out three times to ensure
complete degassing of viscous liquids). Toluene (1.5 mL,
anhydrous/degassed) was added via syringe through the septum, followed by
vigorous stirring and addition of the 3-bromopyridine (0.044 mL, 0.45
mmol, 1.5 eq) was added via syringe. The sealed reaction vessel was
heated to 100 °C in an aluminum-heating block for 2 h. At this time, the
reaction was allowed to cool to room temperature and was diluted with
EtOAc. The resulting heterogeneous mixture was filtered through a pad of
Celite (eluted with additional EtOAc) and the eluent was concentrated
under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (heptanes/ethyl acetate). 2-heteroaryl
tetrahydropyridine product, yield 71 mg, 0.27 mmol, 91%. mp = 73-75 °C.
IR (film): 2976, 1694, 1362, 1336, 1251, 1151 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ
8.57 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.48 (dd, J = 4.7, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.58 (dt, J =
7.8, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.24 (m, 1H), 5.38 (t, J = 3.9 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (m, 2H),
2.32 (m, 2H), 1.90 (m, 2H), 1.12 (s, 9H); 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 153.7,
147.9, 146.9, 137.5, 136.5, 132.6, 122.8, 116.8, 80.8, 44.4, 27.8, 23.8,
23.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vessel used, Suzuki cross-coupling, optimization study, optimized
on catalyst ligand, base, solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Expedient Synthesis of α-Heteroaryl Piperidines Using a Pd-Catalyzed
Suzuki Cross-Coupling-Reduction Sequence
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hesp, Kevin D.; Fernando, Dilinie P.; Jiao, Wenhua; Londregan, Allyn T.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(2), 413-415

