$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Formation of
5-chloro-3-(5-fluoro-4-(methylthio)pyrimidin-2-yl)-1-tosyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine
(15). 2-Chloro-5-fluoro-4-methylsulfanyl-pyrimidine (0.64 g, 3.60 mmol),
5-chloro-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1-tosyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine,
13, (1.30 g, 3.0 mmol) and aqueous Na2CO3 (4.5 mL of 2M solution, 9.0
mmol) were dissolved in DME (14 mL). The mixture was purged with nitrogen
for 15 minutes, treated with Pd(PPh3)4 (0.17 g, 0.15 mmol) and heated in
a pressure tube at 125 °C for 15 minutes. After cooling to room
temperature, the resulting precipitate was filtered and washed with
methanol. Yield: (1.27 g, 94%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.80 (d, J =
2.4, 1H), 8.60 (s, 1H), 8.40 (d, J = 2.4, 1H), 8.25 (d, J = 1.7, 1H),
8.19-8.03 (m, 2H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.1, 2H), 2.74 (s, 3H), 2.39 (s, 3H); MS
(ES+) 449.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM pressure tube used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Novel, First-in-Class, Orally Bioavailable Azaindole
Inhibitor (VX-787) of Influenza PB2
