$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,4-Dioxane (3 mL) was added to a mixture of Pd-(Amphos)2Cl2 (270 mg,
0.43 mmol), 2-fluoro-5-methylpyridin-3-ylboronic acid (1.60 g, 10 mmol),
65a (1.24 g, 8.5 mmol), and KOAc (2.50 g, 26 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (3 mL)
that was heated at 120 °C for 30 min in a microwave reactor. The mixture
was passed through a short plug of diatomaceous earth, washing with
CH2Cl2 (3 × 20 mL). The filtrate was concentrated and purified by silica
gel column chromatography (gradient: 0% → 5% MeOH/CH2Cl2) to give 71m.
Yield (760 mg, 41%), white solid,
4-(2-Fluoro-5-methylpyridin-3-yl)-6-methyl-1,3,5-triazin-2-amine (71m).
LC-MS m/z: 220 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
