$DATUM 5-Methyl-3,4',4''-trihexyl-2,2':5',2''-terthiophene (22). A solution of
21 (3.7 g, 8.6 mmol), 19 (2.8 g, 9.4 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (8.4 g, 25.7 mmol)
in toluene (50 mL) was degassed for 10 min. Pd(PPh3)4 (0.49 g, 0.43 mmol)
was added and the resulting solution was vigorously refluxed overnight
under inert atmosphere. The solution was cooled to room temperature and
diluted with n-hexane, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
crude residue was purified via flash chromatography (SiO2, n-hexane) to
give 22 (4.2 g, 8.1 mmol, 94% yield) as a yellow oil. Rf 0.24 (n-hexane);
IR (neat): 2953, 2926, 2855, 1460, 1440, 1209, 829, 792, 724, 651 cm-1;
1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.95 (d, J= 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J= 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.86
(s, 1H), 6.59 (d, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 2.76 - 2.67 (m, 4H), 2.63 - 2.58 (m,
2H), 2.44 (d, J= 1.0 Hz, 3H), 1.70 - 1.58 (m, 6H), 1.43 - 1.24 (m, 18H),
0.90 (m, 9H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 143.6, 139.5, 139.4, 137.9,
135.7, 134.3, 130.3, 128.4, 128.1, 128.0, 127.0, 119.7, 31.67, 31.65,
31.57, 30.62, 30.53, 30.49, 30.37, 29.34, 29.25, 29.23, 29.21, 29.0,
22.6, 15.3, 14.1; ; LRMS (EI): m/z (%): 514 (100), 515 (38), 516 (20);
