$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-[5-(4 ,4,5,5-Tetramethy[1 ,3,2]dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2,
3-dihydro-indo1-yl]-ethanone (17a). To a solution of 17b (1.86 g, 7.75
mmol) in dioxane (31 mL) were added bis(pinacolato)diboron (3.93 g, 15.5
mmol), Pd(dPPf)2Cl2 (0.57 g, 0.78 mmol), and anhydrous potassium acetate
(3.80 g, 38.7 mmol) under N2. The reaction was heated at 105 °C for 2 h.
Upon cooling to room temperature, water (20 mL) was added to dilute it,
and the resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 Χ 15 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/ n-hexane, 1:50 to 1:2). Pale yellow
solid, yield 2.08 g, 94%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.34 (s, 12H), 2.32
(s, 3H), 3.18 (t, J = 8.45 Hz, 2H), 4.05 (t, J = 8.45 Hz, 2H), 7.62 (s,
1H), 7.67 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.19 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H).
