$DATUM (S)-2-Imino-3,6-dimethyl-6-(4-(5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)thiophen-2-yl)tetrahydropyrimidin-4(1H)-one
(13): To a solution of D4 (20.5 g, 50.3 mmol) in t- BuOH (80 mL) was
added (5-(prop-1-yn-1-yl)pyridin-3-yl)boronic acid (12.3 g, 76.3 mmol), 1
M K2CO3 (76.9 mL, 76.3 mmol) followed by PdCl2(dppf)•CH2Cl2 (1.04 g, 1.26
mmol). The mixture was heated under an atmosphere of nitrogen to 65°C
with stirring for 45 min. After that time, the mixture was cooled to room
temperature and extracted with CH2Cl2 (6 x 100 mL). The combined organic
layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude
product was purified via flash chromatography (SiO2; gradient elution
100:0 to 20:80 hexanes:EtOAc) to afford the intermediate carbamate. The
product was dissolved in TFA/CH2Cl2 (2:3, 250 mL) and the resultant
solution was stirred at RT for 1 hour. The solvent was removed in vacuo.
The crude product was purified via flash chromatography (SiO2; gradient
elution 100:0 to 50:50 CH2Cl2:7 N NH3 in MeOH) to afford 13 free base.
The product was taken up in MeCN (300 mL) and formic acid (6.5 mL) was
added. The solution was then stirred at RT for 3 hours. The solvent was
then removed in vacuo. The resultant solid was further dried in a vacuum
oven at 45 °C for 48 hours to afford 13 as the formate salt. Yield 18.5
g, 94%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.71 (s, 1 H), 8.43 (s, 1 H), 8.08 (s,
1H), 8.06 (s, 1H), 7.82 (s, 1 H), 7.52 (s, 1 H), 3.47 (d, J = 16.4, 1H),
3.24 (d, J = 16.4, 1H), 3.23 (s, 3H), 2.09 (s, 3H), 1.84 (s, 3H), 13C-NMR
(CD3OD, 125 MHz) δ 166.30, 155.84, 149.68, 149.21, 144.81, 137.96,
136.32, 131.23, 123.06, 122.19, 122.01, 90.36, 75.55, 54.18, 43.92,
28.76, 27.79, 2.78. HRMS for C18H19N4OS [M + H]+: calcd: 339.1280; found:
339.1281. LCMS (Conditions E) tR = 1.37 min, m/z 339.1 [M+H]+. [α]D20 -61
(c 0.62, DMSO).
