$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura
couplings:
8-Cyclopropyl-7-naphthalen-1-ylmethyl-5-oxo-2-m-tolyl-5H-thiazolo[3,2-a]pyridine-3-carboxylic
acid methyl ester (6g). Dry MeOH (0.9. ml) was added to pyridone 8 (20mg,
0.043 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (1 mg, 0.004 mmol), KF (5 mg, 0.81 mmol) and
boronic acid (12 mg, 0.085 mmol). The reaction mixture was heated in a
sealed tube by microwave irradiation (MWI) at 100 °C for 10 min. The
resulting mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2, washed with sat. (aq.) NaHCO3
and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic
layers were concentrated under reduced pressure and purification by
parallel flash chromatography[heptane:EtOAc 100:0→0:100].
8-Cyclopropyl-2-(2,3-dihydrobenzo[b][1,4]dioxin-6-yl)-7-naphthalen-1-ylmethyl-5-oxo-5H-thiazolo[3,2-a]pyridine-3-carboxylic
acid methyl ester (6j); (42 mg, 94 % yield); yellow foam. IR (neat) 2979,
1735, 1648, 1471, 1288, 1247, 1068 and 752 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 0.75-0.81 (m, 2H), 1.00-1.07 (m, 2H), 1.75-1.84 (m, 1H), 3.90 (s, 3H),
4.28 (s, 4H), 4.54 (s, 2H), 5.93 (s, 1H), 6.89-6.94 (m, 1H), 7.05-7.14
(m, 2H), 7.20-7.25 (m, 1H), 7.37-7.43 (m, 1H), 7.44-7.51 (m, 2H),
7.75-7.80 (m, 1H), 7.80-7.90 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.8
(2C), 10.9, 36.2, 53.3, 64.2, 64.4, 111.6, 111.8, 117.4, 118.0, 121.6,
121.7, 123.6, 124.8, 125.5, 125.7, 126.2, 127.2, 127.6, 128.5, 128.8,
131.9, 133.9, 134.2, 143.9, 145.2, 146.1, 153.2, 158.8, 161.8. HRMS (FAB)
calcd for [M + H]+ C31H26NO5S+ 524.1526, obsd 524.1532.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design and Synthesis of C-2 Substituted Thiazolo and Dihydrothiazolo
Ring-Fused 2-Pyridones: Pilicides with Increased Antivirulence Activity
