$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (3a)3 :
[16825-51-7] Bis(pinacolato)diboron (2a, 70.0 mg, 0.275 mmol) and sodium
tert-butoxide (26.5 mg, 0.275 mmol) were charged in a dried Schlenk tube
in glovebox, and dissolved in dry THF (1 mL). To the mixture was added
diethylzinc (0.025 mL, 0.025 mmol; 1.0 M hexane solution) at 0ºC, and the
solution was stirred for 30 min at room temperature. To the mixture was
successively added 4-iodoanisole (1a, 58.5 mg, 0.25 mmol) at room
temperature. After the reaction tube was sealed and allowed to warm to
75ºC, the mixture was stirred for 24 h. The reaction was quenched by
aqueous NH4Cl (10 mL), and then extracted with AcOEt (15 mL × 3). The
AcOEt layers were combined and dried over MgSO4, and the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography using AcOEt/hexane (1/20) as eluent. Entry: 20
Product: 4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(3-thienyl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (3t);
Yield: 93%. 1H and 13C NMR were in agreement with the reference13. 1H NMR
(495 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.34 (s, 12H), 7.34 (m, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.41 (d, J =
1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 24.8,
83.6, 125.3, 132.0, 136.4. The carbon directly attached to the boron atom
was not detected, likely due to quadropolar relaxation. EI-MS m/z (%
relative intensity): 210 (M+, 35), 196 (23), 152 (15), 124 (100), 111
(77), 85 (19), 57 (15).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM glovebox used (stage 1), sealed tube used (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Generation, and Synthetic Application of Borylzincate: Borylation
of Aryl Halides and Borylzincation of Benzynes/Terminal Alkyne
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
