$DATUM 1,1,1-Tris(4''-(1,3-dioxolan-2-yl)-3',4'-dihexyl-2,2':5',2''-terthiophen-2-yl)ethane
(S8): A mixture of 1,1,1-tris(5-bromo-2-thienyl)ethane S7 (1.217 g. 2.37
mmol), boronic acid ester S5 (5.482 g, 10.6 mmol), K2CO3 (2.015 g, 14.6
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4(282 mg, 0.244 mmol) in THF/toluene/water (3/3/1, 35
mL) was heated to reflux and stirred for 2 days. After cooling to room
temperature, water (20 mL) was added to the reaction mixture. The aqueous
layer was extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 30 mL). The combined organic
extracts were washed with water (1 × 20 mL) and brine (1 × 20 mL), then
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. After filtration and removal of solvent in
vacuo, the crude product was purified by column chromatography (silica
gel, EtOAc/n-hexane = 1/3) to give product. Yield:93% (3.281g), yellow
orange oil. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.36-7.35 (m, 3H), 7.14 (d, J = 1.3
Hz, 3H), 6.95 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 3H), 6.83 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 3H), 5.87 (s,
3H), 4.12-4.00 (m, 12H), 2.68-2.64 (m, 12H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 1.60-1.50 (m,
12H), 1.42-1.26 (m, 36H), 0.90-0.83 (m, 18H); 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ
152.52, 140.31, 140.25, 139.98, 137.24, 135.66. 130.11, 129.48, 126.17,
124.83, 124.34, 123.25, 100.42, 65.13, 46.83, 33.37, 31.48, 30.72, 30.61,
29.53, 29.51, 28.17, 28.09, 22.61, 22.58, 14.05, 14.04; HRMS
(ESI-Orbitrap): m/z calcd for C83H108O6S9Na, 1511.5524; found, 1511.5531
([M+Na]+).
