$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,4,7,10,13,16-hexa-(1’-N-BOC-pyrrole-2’-yl)-5,6,11,12,17,18-hexaaza-
trinaphthalene (5): Suzuki-Miyaura-coupling 1.835 g (2.140 mmol) of 3
were added into a mixture of 100 ml THF and 40 ml of toluene. 4.516 g
(0.0214 mol) 1-N-BOC-pyrrole-2-boronic acid (4), 0.048 g Aliquat 336,
14.788 g (0.107 mol) K2CO3 in 12 ml of water were added and argon was
bubbled through the reaction-mixture for 1 hour. 0.890 g (0.771 mmol)
tetrakis- (triphenylphosphine)-Pd(0) was added under argon reverse flow.
The reaction mixture was heated to 95 °C for 72 h. The solvents were
removed by distillation. Residual solid was dispersed in water and
extracted by DCM. Purification was performed by column-chromatography
(silica-gel) with a mixture of EtAc, DCM and hexane as eluent in a ratio
of 3 to 3 to 5 (1% triethylamine was added for neutralizing the silica
gel), 2.745 g (2.00 mmol, 93%) of a brown-red solid. Due to acidic
silica-gel BOC-protection groups were partially cleaved off. Therefore
one part was additionally cleaned by HPLC-GPC chromatography for NMR
characterisation, 5 as a dark-red solid.4 1H-NMR (250 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ
7.90 p.p.m. (s, 6H), 7.47 (dd, 6H, J = 3.3 Hz, J = 1.8 Hz), 6.68 (dd, 6H,
J = 3.3 Hz, J = 1.8 Hz), 6.46 (t, 6H, J = 3.3 Hz), 0.91 (s, 54H); 13C-NMR
(300 MHz, CD2Cl2): δ 149.6, 143.3, 143.5, 134.5, 131.7, 131.1, 124.8,
117.1, 110.9, 83.2, 27.7; IR (ATR): 3343, 2981, 2939, 1736, 1479, 1471,
1405, 1403, 1360, 1313, 1255, 1159, 1134, 1117, 1103, 1065, 1051, 968,
850, 810, 767, 721, 669, 598 cm-1; MS (FD, 8 kV) (m/z): [M]+ calcd for
C78H78N12O12, 1,374.59; found 1,374.5; MS (TOF, TCNQ) (m/z): [M]+ calcd
for C78H78N12O12, 1,374.59; found 1,376.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura-coupling, Aliquot 336 used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Triangular Trinuclear Metal-N4 Complexes with High Electrocatalytic
Activity for Oxygen Reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
