$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline (5fh). Under
argon atmosphere, a reaction tube was charged with palladium salt
(Pd(OAc)2 (2.25 mg, 0.01 mmol) or [Pd(allyl)Cl]2 (1.83 mg, 0.005 mmol)),
imidazolium salt 2d (8.66 mg, 0.02 mmol) and cesium carbonate (652 mg, 2
mmol). Then, dioxane (2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred for 15 min
at 90 °C and cooled to room temperature. (This precatalyst formation was
essential for high catalytic performance.) Then, heteroaryl chloride 3
(1.0 mmol) and (hetero)arylboron reagent 4 (1.5 mmol) were added. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h at 90 °C and cooled to room
temperature. Water and saturated Na2CO3 were added and then the resulting
mixture was extracted with ether. The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4. Concentration and purification through silica gel column
chromatography gave desired product 5 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline
(5fh). After the reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h at 100 °C and
cooled to room temperature, CH2Cl2 and 1M NaOH were added. The resulting
mixture was stirred for 1 h at room temperature and extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4. Concentration
and purification through silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc =
5/1) gave the product 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline (5fh).
4-(5-Methylfuran-2-yl)quinoline (5fi). After the reaction mixture was
stirred for 18 h at 90 °C and cooled to room temperature, CH2Cl2 and 1M
NaOH were added. The resulting mixture was stirred for 1 h at room
temperature and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were
dried over Na2SO4. Concentration and purification through silica gel
column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 5/1) gave the product Colorless
oil, 195 mg, (0.93 mmol, 93%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 2.47 (3H, s),
6.23 (1H, d, J = 2.4 Hz), 6.90 (1H, d, J = 3.2 Hz), 7.57-7.60 (1H, m),
7.61 (1H, d, J = 4.6 Hz), 7.71-7.75 (1H, m), 8,13 (1H, d, J = 8.5 Hz),
8.52 (1H, d, J = 8.6 Hz), 8.89 (1H, d, J = 4.6 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): 13.8 (CH3), 108.3 (CH), 113.4 (CH), 117.8 (CH), 124.2 (C), 125.4
(CH), 126.7 (CH), 129.1 (CH), 130.0 (CH), 136.0 (C), 149.0 (C), 149.2
(C), 149.9 (CH), 154.2 (C). IR (ATR): 760, 1020, 1500, 1570 cm-1. HRMS
(EI) m/z calcd for C14H11NO (M+): 209.0841. Found: 209.0831.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
