$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3',3''-Dihexyl-2,2':5',2''-terthiophene-5-carbaldehyde (8). To a N2
degassed suspension 7 (1.67 g, 4.21 mmol),
2-(3-hexylthiophen-2-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (1.75 g,
5.05 mmol) and K2CO3 (2M, 6.31 mL, 12.62 mmol) in 1,2-dimethoxyethane (10
mL) was added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.24 g, 0.21 mmol). The resulting biphasic
solution was sealed and heated to 120 °C for 1 h by microwave heating.
The solution was then poured into pet. ether (100 mL) and washed with
water. The organic layer was dried and concentrated in vacuo to give the
crude product which was purified by automated flash chromatography (SiO2,
n-hexane, 0.5 - 4% EtOAc) to give 8 (1.74 g, 3.91 mmol, 93% yield) as a
yellow oil. Rf 0.18 (n-hexane, 5% EtOAc); IR (neat) 2954, 2925, 2855,
1667, 1458, 1435, 1379, 1226, 1056, 832 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 9.89 (s,
1H), 7.71 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (d, J= 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.20 (d, J= 5.0
Hz, 1H), 6.98 (s, 1H), 6.94 (d, J= 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.85 - 2.75 (m, 4H), 1.74
- 1.60 (m, 4H), 1.47 - 1.27 (m, 12H), 0.92 - 0.86 (m, 6H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 182.6, 146.3, 142.4, 142.1, 140.4, 136.8, 136.6, 130.3, 129.8,
129.2, 129.1, 125.8, 124.3, 31.7, 30.6, 30.3, 29.8, 29.4, 29.20, 29.19,
22.59, 22.58, 14.09, 14.07; LRMS (EI): m/z (%): 444 (100), 445 (26), 446
(15); HRMS (EI): Calcd for C25H32O32S3: 444.1610, found: 444.1611.
