$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.6. Synthesis of Compound 4 To a THF solution (50 mL) of a mixture of 2
(1.0 g, 3.0 mmol) and 3 (1.0 g, 3.3 mmol) were successively added
Pd(PPh3)4 (140 mg, 0.12 mmol) and 2 M aqueous NaOH (6 mL), and the
mixture was refluxed for 12 h under Ar. Then, the reaction mixture was
poured into aqueous NH4Cl, and an aqueous layer separated was extracted
with CH2Cl2. An organic extract was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4,
and evaporated to dryness under reduced pressure, and the residue was
subjected to flash column chromatography on silica gel using hexane as an
eluent. Isolation of 4 as white solid (1.40 g, 93%). Elemental Analysis:
Calcd. for C32H54S2: C, 76.43; H, 10.82. Found: C, 76.03; H, 10.98. 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.09 (s, 2H, Ar-H), 6.97 (s, 2H, Ar-H), 2.78-2.81 (t, J =
7.5 Hz, 4H, CH2), 1.65-1.70 (m, 4H, CH2), 1.26-1.37 (m, 36H, CH2),
0.67-0.89 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H, CH2); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 146.4, 137.1,
123.3, 116.9, 31.9, 31.6, 30.1, 29.7, 29.6, 29.5, 29.4, 29.1, 22.7, 14.1;
MALDI-TOF MS m/z calcd. for C32H54S2 502.3, found 502.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
