$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed Miyaura borylation: To a
solution of appropriate bromoindole (1 equiv) in dioxane anhydrous (2 ml
x mmol) under N2, were added Pd2(dba)3 (0.02 equiv), XPhos
(2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2',4',6'-triisopropylbiphenyl) (0.04 equiv),
KOAc (3 equiv) e bis(pinacolato)diboron (1.2 equiv). The reaction mixture
was stirred at 110 °C for 20 hours under N2, then was cooled at room
temperature, filtrate over Celite and washed with ethyl acetate. To the
reaction mixture was added water. The layers were separated and the
aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x (3 ml x mmol)). The
combined organic phases were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous
sodium sulphate and the solvent evaporated under reduced pressure. The
residue obtained was purified by flash chromatography. Using
4-bromo-1H-indole (4 g, 20.4 mmol). The residue was purified by
flashchromatography (cyclohexane/CH2Cl2 1:1).
4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole (1a) as a
yellowish solid, yield 4.6 g, 19.0 mmol, 93%. TLC (cyclohexane/CH2Cl2
1:1), Rf = 0.31 (UV, CAM). MS (ESI): 244 [M+H]+. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 1.40 (s, 12H), 7.07 (s, 1H), 7.18-7.29 (m, 2H), 7.52 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1
H),7.65 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 8.19 (br s, 1H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ
25.0, 83.4, 104.5, 114.0, 121.3, 124.6, 127.9, 132.5, 135.1 (carbon
adjacent to boron was not observed). 11B NMR (64 MHz, CDCl3 BF3•OEt2): δ
31.4. FTIR (film, cm-1): 3334, 2925, 1609, 1575. M.p.: 264-268°C. Anal.
Calcd. for C14H18BNO2 (243.14): C, 69.17; H, 7.46; N, 5.76. Found: C,
69.12; H, 7.42; N, 5.81.
