$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Suzuki-Miyaura coupling. A schlenk tube (50 mL
in volume) equipped with a stirring bar was heated and cooled under
vacuum and back-filled with argon. Pd(OAc)2 (2.2 mg, 0.01 mmol, 5 mol %),
SPhos (Dicyclohexyl(2',6'-dimethoxy-2-biphenylyl)phosphine, 8.2 mg, 0.02
mmol, 10 mol %) were weighed into the reaction vessel in glovebox.
Heterocyclic MIDA boronate (0.2 mmol, 1.0 eq), THF (5.0 mL), aryl (or
heterocyclic) bromide (0.24 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and 3.0 M aqueous K3PO4
(0.45 mL, 7.5 equiv of base) were introduced under a stream of argon. The
mixture was then stirred at 60 °C for 4-18 h. The reaction was cooled
down before being poured into a separatory funnel containing aqueous NaCl
solution. Extraction with ethyl acetate (3 x 20 mL) was carried out, and
the combined organic extracts were concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
subjected to column chromatography to give the pure product.
3-(5-methylthiophen-3-yl)isoquinolin-1(2H)-one (4f), yield 92%. The
reaction was run for 18 h. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 11.38 (s, 1H),
8.22 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 8.05 (s, 1H), 7.74 - 7.66 (m, 2H), 7.48 (t, J =
6.9 Hz, 1H), 7.41 (s, 1H), 7.00 (s, 1H), 2.51 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 162.54, 140.27, 138.00, 135.23, 134.61, 132.57, 126.64,
126.47, 126.10, 124.76, 124.01, 121.19, 102.08, 14.90. ESI-MS: calculated
[C14H11NOSNa]+: 264.0454, found: 264.0455.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Schlenk tube and glovebox used, Suzuki-Miyaura
cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild Rh(III)-catalyzed C-H activation and annulation with alkyne MIDA
boronates: short, efficient synthesis of heterocyclic boronic acid
derivatives
